    λ_5 =  +0.0334  g_3(λ) =  -1.0345  [spherical]
    λ_6 =  -0.4163  g_3(λ) =  -0.8291  [spherical]
    λ_7 =  -1.0000  g_3(λ) =  -2.0000  [spherical]
    λ_8 =  -1.1840  g_3(λ) =  -2.8774  [spherical]
    λ_9 =  -1.7512  g_3(λ) =  -7.6862  [spherical]
    λ_10 =  -2.4958  g_3(λ) = -20.2807  [spherical]
    λ_11 =  -3.2551  g_3(λ) = -42.8303  [spherical]

  Spectral radius = 5.5823
  The LARGEST eigenvalue is in the HYPERBOLIC regime (g > 0).
  This confirms: G_5 is a hyperbolic graph in the gap function sense.


5. SUSCEPTIBILITY OF G_5
------------------------------------------------------------

  I(G_5, 2) = 793
  I'(G_5, 2) = 1284
  Susceptibility χ = I'/I = 1.619168

  For comparison:
    Regular tournament (H=15, n=5): χ = 7/15 = 0.467
    Transitive tournament (H=1, n=5): χ = 0
    G_5 itself: χ = 1.6192


